# Vercel only builds the `frontend` Root Directory. Everything below is
# excluded from the CLI upload so the source tarball stays under the 100 MB cap.
# Vercel reinstalls dependencies and rebuilds on its own servers, so local
# node_modules / build outputs never need to be uploaded.
#
# NOTE: keep patterns conservative. Do NOT use broad globs like **/lib/ —
# that would wrongly exclude frontend/src/lib (app source code).

# Sibling monorepo projects not built by this Vercel project.
# NOTE: do NOT exclude landing/ — it is its own Vercel project (Root Directory
# `landing`) that deploys via git, and .vercelignore is shared repo-wide, so
# excluding it strips the landing project's source and breaks its deploys.
# landing/ is small source (no committed build artifacts), so leaving it in the
# dashboard CLI upload is well under the 100 MB cap.
operator/
engine/
functions/
extension/
docs/

# Dependencies (reinstalled on Vercel)
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Frontend build output (rebuilt on Vercel)
frontend/.next/
frontend/out/

# Logs and local scratch files
*.log
logs*.txt
*-output.txt
captured-*.json
